Z||000000||BC-GT||10-21-2001||07:22 PM||||Need any info and part numbers for these three parts. Up here in Canada I can't seem to find them. GM has a listing for the grommets but they are $24 bucks each(WTF!) They also have a listing for a oil filler cap but it's the push on round type(not correct, it will leak water if pressure washed!)<BR> Canadian Tire here has a good assortment of Help(Motormite) parts but no application guide to go with them. I'm pretty sure they have something that might fit.<BR> Even an OD and ID of the pieces(valve cover holes) would help.<BR>Thanks.<BR>PS. what kind of oil cap does the Fiero store sell. IE: is it a proper fit with the 2 tangs or just a round push on type that leaves the 2 tangs exposed somewhat.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Rick 88||10-21-2001||11:50 PM||||I was not able to purchase a factoy valve cover grommet here. I did find a similar one, with an angled shape, in the HELP section of an auto parts store. I had to trim it to fit snugly but it was only a couple of bucks instead of $24! Just take your PCV with you to compare the opening size and purchase one with a wider flange for aluminum valvecovers.<P>You might try looking at some similar GM engines in a wrecking yard to find a factory oil cap. I think it is a pretty standard design.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
